[{"name":"mcp__codex_apps__airtable_delete_page","description":"Add structured data to ChatGPT

Deletes a page from an interface, given its pageId.
Standalone forms, and pages that have no published version yet, are removed immediately. A
page that has its own published version is instead staged for removal in the working draft,
staying visible to end users until the interface is published.
The agent MUST ask the user for explicit confirmation before calling this tool.
Page deletion is destructive and should not be performed without the user's go-ahead.
Use list_pages_for_base to find the appropriate pageId.
After deleting, only offer to run publish_interface (with the user's
confirmation) when the removal was staged — i.e. the page had its own published version. If it
was removed immediately (a standalone form, or a page with no published version), the deletion
already took effect for end users, so do not suggest publishing. This tool is part of plugin `Airtable`.

