--- README ---
# PostgreSQL recovery tooling

This folder holds read-only planning and dump-rewrite helpers for archived PG18/FalkorDB salvage inputs. It does not restore a database, delete source artifacts, or mutate live CNPG clusters.

## Safety boundary

- Preserve source artifacts in place. These helpers inventory and plan against existing files only.
- Fail closed on duplicate logical inputs unless `-PreferredRoot` explicitly names one of the supplied archive roots.
- Do not point any command here at a live production database without an explicit operator decision.
- `sql/soil-current-wins.sql` is intentionally manual and targets a staged schema named `recovery_soil_current`.

## Read-only inventory

Record file availability, size, timestamp, and checksum without copying or altering archives:

```powershell
powershell -NoProfile -File .\tools\postgresql\Get-RecoveryArchiveInventory.ps1 `
  'C:\_backups\coldaine-rebuild\20260708-013237' `
  'C:\_backups\coldaine-rebuild\20260711-232908-pre-teardown'
```

Checksums come from each root's `SHA256SUMS.txt` when available and fall back to SHA-256 hashing only for relevant files absent from the manifest.

## Collision-safe recovery plan

Generate a local import plan from both archive roots, explicitly preferring the July 11 archive when a logical dump exists in both roots:

```powershell
powershell -NoProfile -File .\tools\postgresql\New-PgRecoveryPlan.ps1 `
  -Root 'C:\_backups\coldaine-rebuild\20260708-013237', 'C:\_backups\coldaine-rebuild\20260711-232908-pre-teardown' `
  -PreferredRoot 'C:\_backups\coldaine-rebuild\20260711-232908-pre-teardown'
```

The July 8 root remains the fallback for logical dumps that exist only there. Without `-PreferredRoot`, any duplicate logical PostgreSQL or FalkorDB dump fails closed rather than guessing.

## Dump rewriting

`Convert-PgDump.ps1` rewrites a logical dump stream for role-scoped CNPG import without materializing rewritten SQL on disk.

- `Standard` strips ownership, grants, extension DDL, database creation, and session-role statements.
- `Corpus` retains extension-owned catalog rows under an elevated role before returning to the app owner.
- `TodoCards` additionally skips Timescale-owned statements and COPY blocks.

```powershell
powershell -NoProfile -File .\tools\postgresql\Convert-PgDump.ps1 `
  -InputFile 'C:\_backups\coldaine-rebuild\20260711-232908-pre-teardown\postgres\pg18-soil.sql' `
  -Role soil `
  -Profile Standard
```

## Soil merge helper

After loading historical Soil data into `recovery_soil_current`, apply `sql/soil-current-wins.sql` deliberately so current live rows win on natural-key conflicts.

